# ESP32 & ATmega328p Coprocessor Quadcopter UAV

Welcome to the main repository for the ESP32-based Quadcopter UAV, featuring an ATmega328p coprocessor. 

In this architecture, the ESP32 handles high-level flight dynamics, complex computations, and wireless communication. The ATmega328p acts as a dedicated coprocessor handling low-level, real-time hardware tasks such as precise motor PWM generation and sensor interfacing. Both microcontrollers are programmed strictly in baremetal C/C++ to ensure maximum performance and minimal overhead.

This guide covers how to set up the official development environments required to view the hardware designs, compile the firmware from scratch, and flash the boards.

