## 2. Baremetal Toolchain Setup

### ESP32 Setup (ESP-IDF)
To compile the high-level flight controller firmware for the ESP32, you need the official Espressif IoT Development Framework (ESP-IDF). 

For the most up-to-date, OS-specific instructions, always refer to the [Official ESP-IDF Get Started Guide](https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/latest/esp32/get-started/index.html).

**General Linux/macOS Command Line Installation:**
```bash
# Create a directory for ESP-IDF
mkdir -p ~/esp
cd ~/esp

# Clone the official repository
git clone --recursive [https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf.git](https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf.git)

# Run the official installation script
cd esp-idf
./install.sh esp32


// ENVIRONMENT SETUP
# On Linux/macOS
. $HOME/esp/esp-idf/export.sh

# On Windows (Command Prompt)
%USERPROFILE%\esp\esp-idf\export.bat

# Build the project
idf.py build

# Flash to the board and open the serial monitor (replace YOUR_PORT with your COM/tty port)
idf.py -p (YOUR_PORT) flash monitor

make -> make flash(same method for ATmega328p)

